'''Ngadjuri''' is an [[language death|extinct]] [[Australian Aboriginal language]] formerly spoken by the [[Ngadjuri people]] of [[South Australia]], whose [[traditional owner|traditional lands]] covered roughly {{convert|11,500|mi2|order=flip}}, embracing [[Angaston, South Australia|Angaston]] and [[Freeling, South Australia|Freeling]] in the south and running northwards to [[Clare, South Australia|Clare]], [[Crystal Brook, South Australia|Crystal Brook]], [[Gladstone, South Australia|Gladstone]] up to [[Carrieton]] and [[Orroroo, South Australia|Orroroo]]  in the [[Flinders Ranges]].

